Z||000011||EdsB52||08-13-2001||08:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR>[B][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"I started this thread because I am tired of what has been happening on this forum and I didn't want to add to another thread and appear to be supporting any one individual."<P>If you didn't want to add another thread, then why did you? The only person mentioned in your thread is me, while others enjoyed the protection of "There are some members(who shall remain unnamed) that just don't want to let go." Maybe the reason the list is unavailable is that you would have to name yourself and the person registered as your daughter (if different). <P>"I am tired of the bickering,as I am sure many others are.If one member doesn't like another they should ignore them and not try to draw them into an arguement that the rest of the forum is almost forced to watch like the soap operas."<P>Exactly, I've made peace with everyone but Archie, who continues to blast away, but things are fine other than that and now this thread. Honestly, Hugh, I think most forum members will agree that you could have spent your time more constructively in the soap opera thread, where levity reigns supreme. Pick a role and join in.<P>"Again,I support no one I am just tired of the fighting."<P>Actually that's not true. I'll share with the rest of forum our history. You advertised in the MAll that you were looking for a complete tan seat belt assy for both sides. I had a parts car, knew that I had one there, and told you I would sell it for $30 including shipping. I thought shipping would be negligible so I threw it in. Anyway, Hugh sends me the money, I go to ship the belts, but find it's $18 for shipping. I go ahead and ship them for $18 and tell Hugh about it, but also told him $30 was the arrangement so it's fine. A week later I get another check from Hugh for $18, so I email him back to tell him that the original deal was $30 including shipping and that I'm going to shred the check, which I did. In summary, both Hugh and I acted with great character and at that point I had absolute respect for him. He was actually my favorite forum member at that point, as I thought he acted above par for submitting what was the unexpectedly exorbitant postage without petition, which I shredded. Now I'll tie this together with why Hugh is taking sides. Then the dark days incident occurred and Hugh was all over my crap, but since I had great respect for him I let it slide. He was all over my crap because he and Archie have a good friendship and Hugh felt the noble desire to defend Archie. Now that Archie is back at it and is unsuccessful, Hugh is revisiting this stuff in the hopes of sparking more hostility.<P>"Edsb52 with his long posts have upset more than a few people."<P>I think we've all written long, boring posts.<P>"You know Ed is going to write a novel long response, someone will be offended by it, and all the quoting will begin AGAIN."<P>Why stir the pot, unless you want it to start up again? Again, my name is the only mentioned amongst all the players in your post.<BR> <BR>"Honestly the best thing to do is IGNORE. Fights can be picked at anytime, but it takes more to keep them going... Who cares who quotes who, who offends who, That person just hurt themself by posting it, you don't need to re-inforce and reflect their idiocy."<P>Fierolisa, I'm not flaming you here but this stirs the pot more. If ignoring is best, why not ignore this thread? You'll ask the same of me, and I'll answer with the fact that Archie, Hugh, and a couple others are keeping the crap going. I want it to end, but you can't expect me to sit here and take this much longer. The thread that Archie started was obviously about me. If necessary I'll prove why, but I'd rather we all let this go.<P>"Way to go Dad!!!!! Do you feel better? I hope so."<P>Eleven minutes after the initiation of this thread, the person claiming to be Hugh's daughter posted this:<P>"Way to go Dad!!!!! Do you feel better? I hope so."<P>Six minutes later, Hugh posted this:<P>"Lisa,I'm trying to make it better.If you go into something thinking "it can't get better",then it won't."<P>Oreif wrote:<P>"I don't like the way Ed also provokes people. I think his posts are ment to start an argument. There are many times when someone posts a response agreeing with him and soon he changes his story. Ever since the time when he contributed to the shut-down of the forum, I would just ignore his long posts."<P>For someone that actually extended support yesterday (if I remember right) and did what I thought were measures to help the healing of relationships, this is unexpected. Oreif, do you think this helps or stirs the pot?<P>To conclude, I would ask, Cliff, each member, and the forum as a whole what they want. I've made amends with all of the members except Archie, and I've let every one of those people have the last word (not all required it). I think the relationship between Archie and I is irrevocably damaged and that we should just ignore each other. Again, what do you guys want individually and as a whole? I've offered peace, but some appear to not want that. Maybe there's a winding down process and some people need to taper off with the insults and attacks, but it's now time. One or two people can take this forum down; let's not let it happen. Even though we are thousands of miles apart, we are still symbiotic in ways. People are quick to jam me, but tend to leave others alone as if they have special privilege. That doesn't bother me, just an observation. <P>I'm now going to appeal to the other members that want this forum and want it friendly. Maybe you can peacefully recommend to those that are trying to either keep these hostilities going, or that are trying to relive what happened a month and a half ago, that they should drop it. No more subtleties about blowing wind or any snide remarks. I'm not going to sit here much longer; I'm going to jump back. It's your forum, direct it the way you want it. Let’s applaud My7fieros for starting that hilarious soap opera thread. Peace.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DRH||08-13-2001||11:07 PM||||Ed,<P>Why not just takes Hugh's statements at face value? While his approach could be argued, his intentions seem to be honorable. You seem to be parsing through his words looking for a hidden agenda. If you look hard enough you can find stuff like that anywhere. For example; you ask Hugh "if you didn't want to add another thread, then why did you?". What Hugh said was "I didn't want to add <B>to</B> another thread". Did you simply misread what Hugh said or should I assume you did it intentionally to make Hugh look bad? See what I mean?<P>Later, David.<BR>||||reg||1
